\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{The cube category with connections is defined by its PRO presentation (Grandis–Mauri: free strict monoidal category on an interval object with connections), included in the kernel as a \em{shape for horn-filling models only} (cubical Kan complexes, cubical (∞,1)-categories after Doherty–Kapulkin–Lindsey–Sattler, and, via connections as companion/conjoint squares, equipments with all companions). It carries no Segal-style structure because it has no spines.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Segal conditions need shapes that contain their own subdivisions (\code{[2] ⊃ [1] ∨ [1]}); cubes only have \code{I^n}. The library's root is Segal-style, so cubes are auxiliary.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen; \code{later} for any use beyond definition.}
}
